Tools for Actions ATJ213x (ATJ2135/ATJ2137) based players
==========================================================

Host tools and target helpers used to bring up and maintain Rockbox on
ATJ213x devices, mainly the iriver E150. Unless noted otherwise they
build with "make" in their directory; the USB tools need libusb-1.0 and
usually root (or a udev rule) to open the device.

The boot ROM's recovery mode (ADFU, USB 10d6:ff96) is the entry point of
most of them. The E150 enters it when Vol+ and Vol- are held while the USB
cable is plugged in (with the Rockbox bootloader installed), or when no
firmware boots.


adfuload/
    Loads and runs code over the boot ROM's ADFU protocol: a stage 1 (a
    first stage from the vendor tools, e.g. ADEC_N63.BIN, -e encodes it the
    way the boot ROM wants) and optionally a stage 2 binary of your own,
    e.g. a Rockbox build. It also reads memory and registers to files (-r,
    before or with -R after stage 1) and writes registers (-w), which helps
    to compare the hardware state of different boot paths.

    test_binary/ holds small bare metal test programs to load with it.

atjboottool/
    Unpacks and builds firmware update files. Decrypts FWU files to AFI
    archives and encrypts them back (--fwu-encrypt, with the keys of an
    existing FWU), unpacks AFI and FW archives, replaces files in an AFI or
    in the LFI firmware image (FWIMAGE.FW) with the checksums the boot
    code checks recomputed.

    --e150-patch builds the Rockbox installer for the E150: it puts the
    Rockbox bootloader (bootloader.e150 as built or downloaded, or the plain
    bootloader.bin) into an original E150.HEX update so that it starts in
    place of WELCOME.BIN. Copy the result to the player's root and let
    the original firmware's updater install it. With the bootloader:
    Rockbox starts from the internal flash, from the SD card when it is not
    there (Vol+ held: the SD card first), Vol- boots the original firmware,
    Vol+ and Vol- with the USB cable plugged in the ADFU recovery mode.

atjflash/
    Recovery: replays an ADFU flashing session recorded from the vendor's
    ProductTool, comparing every response of the device with the recording
    and stopping on the first difference. usbmon_adfu.py turns a Linux
    usbmon capture (pcap) of such a session into the replay script, and
    lists the commands of a capture. The recording is the user's own, of
    their own device and firmware.

nanddump/
    Raw dump of the NAND (data and spare, no ECC processing) over hwstub:
    atjnanddump loads helper.bin (built with a mipsel cross compiler,
    CROSS=mipsel-elf-) into SDRAM and reads pages with it; only read
    commands are sent to the flash. atjftl.py rebuilds the original
    firmware's logical disks from such a dump (-l lists zones and disks,
    -d N extracts one, -e applies the ECC with atjbch.py).

ftltest/
    Host test harness for the Rockbox NAND FTL
    (firmware/target/mips/atj213x/ftl-atj213x.c) against a raw NAND dump,
    with power cuts and NAND failures injected. See ftltest/README.

sdboot/
    Booting from an SD card: a boot sector and a second stage that do what
    the original second stage boot loader does (SDRAM and cache setup) and
    then load a payload from the card. The boot ROM tries the card when the
    internal flash does not boot. mksdboot.py builds the card image (sd) or
    a stage 2 for adfuload (adfu). Needs a mipsel cross compiler.


Related: the ATJ modules of hwstub (utils/hwstub/tools/lua/atj*), the
register descriptions in utils/regtools/desc/regs-atj213x.xml.
